Title: Low Tide
Author: Dana Reyes
Draft date: October 1, 2026

INT. LAB - NIGHT

Rain on the roof.

MAYA
Listen. The pumps stopped an hour ago.

CUT TO:

EXT. ROOF - NIGHT

Wind tears at the antenna. Theo grips the rail with both hands.

THEO
What was that? Tell me you heard it too.

INT. HALL - DAY

Footsteps echo down the long empty hall.

INT. KITCHEN - MORNING

The kettle clicks off. Maya pours two cups and slides one across.

MAYA
I told you twice.

EXT. STREET - DUSK

Cars crawl past the harbor wall, headlights on.
